Kernel_validateUserOp
├── when the caller is not the EntryPoint
│   └── when the caller is not the account itself
│       └── it should revert with Unauthorized error
└── when the caller is the EntryPoint or self
    ├── given the validation mode has enable flag set
    │   ├── given the nonce is invalid
    │   │   └── it should revert with InvalidNonce error
    │   ├── given the enable signature is invalid
    │   │   └── it should return SIG_VALIDATION_FAILED
    │   └── given the enable signature is valid and nonce is unused
    │       ├── it should install the packages from the signature
    │       ├── it should increment the nonce
    │       └── it should continue with userOp validation using the remaining signature
    ├── given the validation type is ROOT
    │   ├── given the root is not set
    │   │   └── it should use the fallback validator
    │   ├── given the root is set to a permission type
    │   │   └── it should use permission validation for root
    │   ├── when the signature is valid
    │   │   ├── it should return 0 for success
    │   │   └── it should allow any callData without restrictions
    │   └── when the signature is invalid
    │       └── it should return SIG_VALIDATION_FAILED
    ├── given the validation type is VALIDATOR
    │   ├── given the validator is not installed
    │   │   └── it should revert with InvalidVid error
    │   └── given the validator is installed
    │       ├── when validator returns empty data
    │       │   └── it should return SIG_VALIDATION_FAILED when validator returns empty data
    │       ├── given the callData selector is in the allowed list and hook is address1
    │       │   ├── when the validator signature is valid
    │       │   │   └── it should return 0 for success
    │       │   └── when the validator signature is invalid
    │       │       └── it should return SIG_VALIDATION_FAILED
    │       ├── given the callData selector is in the allowed list and hook is not address1
    │       │   ├── when the callData does not use executeUserOp wrapper
    │       │   │   └── it should revert with UnauthorizedCallData error
    │       │   └── when the callData uses executeUserOp wrapper
    │       │       ├── it should set the validation hook for later execution
    │       │       └── it should continue with signature validation
    │       ├── given the callData selector is not directly allowed
    │       │   ├── when the callData does not use executeUserOp wrapper
    │       │   │   └── it should revert with UnauthorizedCallData error
    │       │   └── when the callData uses executeUserOp wrapper
    │       │       ├── given the inner selector is in the allowed list
    │       │       │   ├── it should set the validation hook for later execution
    │       │       │   └── it should continue with signature validation
    │       │       └── given the inner selector is not in the allowed list
    │       │           └── it should revert with UnauthorizedCallData error
    │       └── given a validation hook is configured
    │           └── it should store the hook in transient storage for executeUserOp
    ├── given the validation type is PERMISSION
    │   ├── given the permission is not installed
    │   │   └── it should revert with InvalidVid error
    │   └── given the permission is installed
    │       ├── given the callData selector restrictions are not met
    │       │   └── it should revert with UnauthorizedCallData error
    │       ├── given the signature count does not match policies plus one
    │       │   └── it should revert with InvalidSignature error
    │       ├── when all policies pass validation
    │       │   ├── when the signer signature is valid
    │       │   │   └── it should return 0 for success
    │       │   └── when the signer signature is invalid
    │       │       └── it should return SIG_VALIDATION_FAILED
    │       ├── when any policy fails validation
    │       │   └── it should return SIG_VALIDATION_FAILED
    │       └── given multiple policies are installed
    │           └── it should iterate all policies in the loop
    ├── given the validation mode is replayable
    │   ├── it should compute userOpHash without chainId
    │   └── it should allow the same signature to be valid across different chains
    ├── given the validation mode is not replayable
    │   ├── it should compute userOpHash with chainId
    │   └── it should make the signature invalid on different chains
    ├── when missingAccountFunds is greater than zero
    │   ├── it should attempt to transfer the funds to the EntryPoint
    │   └── it should not revert if the transfer fails
    ├── when validation returns time bounded data
    │   ├── given validAfter is in the future
    │   │   └── it should return the validAfter in the validation result
    │   ├── given validUntil is in the past
    │   │   └── it should return the validUntil in the validation result
    │   └── given both validAfter and validUntil are set
    │       └── it should return intersected validation data
    └── when multiple validations return time bounded data
        └── it should intersect all validation results
